\f1\fs22 Captain Denver tapped on one of the parlour doors. Both slid open; six Elvi in uniform marched in and took positions guarding all the doors and windows. Five more Elvi of varying series, wearing performance ponchos\'97one with a guitar casually and confidently slung over her shoulder\'97stepped into the room, and slid the doors closed. The room quietened, as any auditorium about to hear an Elvi song would. The performers took positions a step in front of Captain Denver. They looked left and right at each other\'92s feet and uniformly spaced themselves out, like grade school kids on stage for the year-end pageant.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>The guitarist strummed up some chords, while the singers swayed into the mood. Then, with melodies and harmonies that would gird the loins of gods, make psychopaths weep and sociopaths repent of arson, they sang:\
