<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>On conclusion, the performers approached the dining table and filched everything they could possibly carry. The guitarist laid his instrument flat to make a tray of it, and piled food on top. With mouths full and morsels, dribbles and clumps of food falling from their arms and fingerboards, they left.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Unaccustomed to receiving threats, Sarah gulped and blinked. She stared at Tony with withering accusation.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91Don\'92t look at me, I didn\'92t write that!\'92 Tony protested, but in truth, he\'92d been working up something similar with the musos all afternoon.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Captain Denver made labour over writing carefully in his notebook, then neatly detached a page, and presented it to Sarah, who half-expected it to be a bill for the food. What chilled her more than any Cloudborne\'97let alone an Elvi\'97expecting prompt payment from an Airborne, were the actual words on the note:\
